The Flick compiler and toolchain

Usage: flick [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check    Check Flick source files and report diagnostics
  build    Compile the project, or the given files, to ES modules
  fmt      Format Flick source files in place
  test     Run the tests of the project's test root
  ffi      Bindings to npm packages from their `.d.ts`
  new      Create a project in a new directory
  init     Add a project to the working directory; existing files are kept
  run      Build the app as JavaScript and run its `main`
  dev      Rebuild on changes and replace the running app after its shutdown
  clean    Remove the build artifacts of the project
  install  Install the dependencies with the pinned pnpm
  add      Add npm packages to the dependencies
  remove   Remove direct dependencies
  update   Update dependencies within the ranges of `package.json`
  deps     Show the installed dependencies and their Flick interfaces
  pack     Build a release package and an npm tarball of it
  schema   Static schemas of codecs
  doc      Write documentation of the public API
  explain  Explain a diagnostic code
  doctor   Check the compiler, Node.js, pnpm and the runtime
  inspect  Print a representation of a module: AST, typed IR, JS, TS, interface or source mapping
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --diagnostics <DIAGNOSTICS>  Format of diagnostics on stderr [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --color <COLOR>              Colorize human-readable output [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --quiet                      Print less service output
      --verbose                    Print more service output
      --project <PATH>             Project directory or its `flick.toml`; by default the nearest `flick.toml` from the working directory upwards
      --warnings-as-errors         Treat warnings as errors
  -h, --help                       Print help
  -V, --version                    Print version
